From ef169b9a39572fa3acc2d34502b9999e7f2c564f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Toma=C5=BE=20Vajngerl?= <tomaz.vajngerl@collabora.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 22:35:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Remove the lp_solve solver, which CoinMP makes redundant
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Lpsolve solver and the CoinMP solver are both used for the same
thing: a linear model, with optional integer variables by branch
and bound. CoinMP (CLP plus CBC) is the more capable and better
maintained of the two, so the lp_solve one adds a second bundled
dependency and a parallel copy of the solver code for no capability
the other lacks.

Remove the LpsolveSolver component, the bundled lp_solve external
(and its colamd dependency, which only lp_solve used), and all the
build, configure, packaging and license references to them.

A document may still name com.sun.star.comp.Calc.LpsolveSolver as
its engine. SolverSettings now reads that name as the CoinMP
solver, which solves the same model, so such documents keep
working.

The Calc solver test that exercised the engine now uses CoinMP. Its
knapsack model has a single optimal total value of 6987, which fills
the weight capacity of 1000 exactly and which CoinMP finds. The
lp_solve run had returned a suboptimal 6981, so the test now expects
the true optimum.

The build setup changes only take effect after re-running autogen.

Signed-off-by: Tomaž Vajngerl <tomaz.vajngerl@collabora.co.uk>
Change-Id: Ia14d8c491779873da6b0157aa524056275adf8f5
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.collaboraoffice.com/c/online/+/3810
Reviewed-by: Miklos Vajna <vmiklos@collabora.com>
Tested-by: Jenkins CPCI <releng@collaboraoffice.com>
(cherry picked from commit e77738a7ca7d44fd9d1f852e26d46e3a6d60467b)
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.libreoffice.org/c/core/+/208038
Tested-by: Jenkins
Reviewed-by: Xisco Fauli <xiscofauli@libreoffice.org>
---
 sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx b/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx
index b7735a7..e404dae 100644
--- a/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx
+++ b/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx
@@ -116,8 +116,9 @@ void ScSolverSettingsObj::testXSolverSettings()
     xSolverModel->setSuppressDialog(true);
     xSolverModel->solve();
 
-    // The correct solution value is 6981 (using LpsolveSolver)
-    CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL(static_cast<double>(6981), xSheet->getCellByPosition(6, 6)->getValue());
+    // The optimal total value for this knapsack is 6987, which fills the weight
+    // capacity of 1000 exactly.
+    CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL(static_cast<double>(6987), xSheet->getCellByPosition(6, 6)->getValue());
 
     // Check objective function and variable cells
     testCellAddress(aObjCell, xSolverModel->getObjectiveCell());
